      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm not sure what you mean by \"goblins whispering in the corners of your mind,\" but I'll stick to the grain direction for now. You mentioned the grain direction of the pins might help—can you explain how the orientation of the fibers relative to the paring stroke affects the splintering issue? Also, would a sharper bevel angle on the chisel itself help with the cleaner shear you're talking about?",
      "source": "evaluator"
